cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OEV in your research, please cite it."
title: "OEV: a small System One decision model"
authors:
  - family-names: Dhruv
    given-names: Divyanshu
    website: "https://github.com/divyanshudhruv"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-23"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/divyanshudhruv/oev"
url: "https://huggingface.co/divyanshudhruv/oev-typed"
keywords:
  - decision-model
  - system-one
  - calibration
  - classification
abstract: >-
  OEV is a small System One decision model. It reads a state,
  scores typed questions (choice, noul, score) over it in a
  single forward pass, and returns calibrated probability
  distributions. At 184M parameters it matches or exceeds
  larger published decision models on shared public benchmarks
  while running at 22 ms per decision.
